cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'CHIMERA: build, run and govern teams of AI agents'
message: 'If you refer to CHIMERA in written work, please cite it using these details.'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: M
    given-names: Hammad
    alias: HammadM-dev
repository-code: 'https://github.com/HammadM-dev/chimera'
url: 'https://github.com/HammadM-dev/chimera'
abstract: >-
  CHIMERA is a local-first desktop application for building, running and
  governing teams of AI agents. Agents are joined on a visual canvas and run
  against any model provider — hosted, gateway or local. Every model call and
  every tool call passes through a governor that enforces capability
  allowlists, egress allowlists, spend and step caps, and human approval for
  irreversible actions. Tool output is handled strictly as data rather than as
  instructions, with a prompt-injection corpus run against every tool-enabled
  role on each commit. Workflows, run traces and credentials remain on the
  user's machine; credentials are held in the operating system keychain and
  never in the database, logs or traces.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agent-orchestration
  - multi-agent-systems
  - large-language-models
  - ai-safety
  - prompt-injection
  - workflow-automation
  - local-first
  - desktop-application
  - model-context-protocol
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-08-30'
